## How It Works

### Form Inputs
| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Title** | Optional label for the entry |
| **Text Area** | Main body of text to save (required) |

### Buttons
| Button | Action |
|---|---|
| **💾 Save** | Saves the current input to `localStorage` |
| **⬇ Download** | Downloads the current input as a `.txt` file |
| **✕ Clear** | Wipes the form fields |
| **✕ (per entry)** | Deletes an individual saved entry |

### Key Features
- **Persistent Storage** — Entries are saved to `localStorage`, so they survive page reloads
- **Entry List** — All saved entries display below the form with timestamps and delete buttons
- **Download Option** — Convert your current input into a `.txt` file for local storage
- **Toast Notifications** — Feedback messages appear at the bottom for save/delete/clear actions
- **Entry Counter** — Shows how many entries are currently stored
- **XSS Protection** — User text is escaped before being inserted into the DOM
- **Responsive Design** — Works on mobile and desktop screens

